There exist an instance of the PMC bandit problem with minimal gap $\dr{}$ such that the expected regret of any consistent algorithm\footnote{An algorithm is called consistent if for any problem and any $\alpha>0$, the regret of the algorithm is $R(t)=o(t^\alpha)$ as $t\to\infty$.} is bounded by 
\begin{equation}
\liminf_{t\to\infty} \frac{R(t)}{\log t} \ge \frac{\bar\Nitems^2(\Narms-\Nbatch)}{4\dr{}} \enspace.
\end{equation}
